[h1]Your pawnshop's whale-girl maid assistant[/h1]
Chat with Xiaojing and ask her to organize the pawnshop using live game tools. Includes a pixel-art character portrait and cover. Chinese and English follow the language selected in the game automatically; other languages use English.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Click the portrait to chat. F6 hides or shows it; F7 opens settings.
[*]OpenAI-compatible API connection with editable URL, API key, model and model-list fetching. Bring your own API service and key; no API credits are included.
[*]Editable system prompt with restore-default and test-chat preview. Default: a lively maid who calls you Master, with no emoji or emoticons unless requested. Custom prompts are preserved when switching language.
[*]Move items to the counter, storage, archives, trash bin and machine inputs through native game rules. Supports nested folders, bags, storage pages and machine compartments.
[*]Read the current customer's intent, remaining purchase budget, preferences, refusal rules and barter/procurement/gunsmith requirements. Check specific items against buying preferences and the current budget estimate.
[/list]

[h2]Examples[/h2]
"Put the food in my inventory on the counter."
"What does this customer want, and how much budget do they have left?"
"Find suitable items, but tell me before moving them."

[h2]Setup and privacy[/h2]
Enable the mod in the Mods menu, review its network capability, restart, then configure your own API provider in F7. Default endpoint: https://api.deepseek.com ; default model: deepseek-flash. A tool-calling model is required for game operations.

Network requests start only when you fetch models, send a test or use the assistant. Game information queried by tools is sent to your configured provider. Remembered API keys are stored in plain text in your own local mod-data folder; disable Remember API key and save for a session-only key. The uploaded package contains no API keys, personal settings, saves, account data, game DLLs, debug symbols or research caches.

[h2]Scope[/h2]
The assistant does not complete trades, select dialogue options, unlock containers, spawn items or start machines. Partial moves and native automatic processing follow the game. Stopping cancels later actions; completed moves remain.

Beta v0.6.0, built against application 0.46D / VERSION 100-Rev3. Automated tests simulate game state and HTTP; gameplay and provider compatibility need player testing. Independent fan mod, not an official DeepSeek product. Character and cover artwork generated with AI from a supplied character reference.
